1803:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** 
1804:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** /*********************************************************************
1805:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1806:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *       SEGGER_SYSVIEW_Start()
1807:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1808:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Function description
1809:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Start recording SystemView events.
1810:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1811:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    This function is triggered by the SystemView Application on connect.
1812:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    For single-shot or post-mortem mode recording, it needs to be called
1813:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    by the application.
1814:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1815:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Additional information
1816:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    This function enables transmission of SystemView packets recorded
1817:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    by subsequent trace calls and records a SystemView Start event.
1818:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1819:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    As part of start, a SystemView Init packet is sent, containing the system
1820:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    frequency. The list of current tasks, the current system time and the
1821:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    system description string is sent, too.
1822:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
1823:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Notes
1824:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    SEGGER_SYSVIEW_Start and SEGGER_SYSVIEW_Stop do not nest.
1825:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    When SEGGER_SYSVIEW_CAN_RESTART is 1, each received start command
1826:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    records the system information. This is required to enable restart
1827:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of recordings when SystemView unexpectedly disconnects without sending
1828:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    a stop command before.
1829:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** */
1830:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** void SEGGER_SYSVIEW_Start(void) {
