2520:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2521:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Function description
2522:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Record a system-heap allocation event.
2523:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2524:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Parameters
2525:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    pHeap       - Pointer to heap where allocation was made.
2526:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    pUserData   - Pointer to allocated user data.
2527:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    UserDataLen - Size of block allocated to hold user data, excluding any metadata.
2528:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2529:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Additional information
2530:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    The user data must be correctly aligned for the architecture, which
2531:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    typically requires that the alignment is at least the alignment
2532:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of a double or a long long.  pUserData is, therefore, compressed by
2533:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    shrinking as IDs are compressed, controlled by the specific setting
2534:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT.
2535:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2536:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    In the same way, UserDataLen must reflect the size of the allocated
2537:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    block, not the allocation size requested by the application.  This
2538:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    size is also subject to compression, controlled by the specific setting
2539:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT.
2540:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2541:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    As an example, assume the allocator is running on a Cortex-M device
2542:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    with SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT set to 2 (the word alignment of the device).
2543:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    If a user requests an allocation of 5 bytes, a hypothetical heap
2544:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    allocator could allocate a block with size 32 bytes for this.  The value
2545:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of UserDataLen sent to SystemView for recording should be 32, not 5,
2546:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    and the 32 is compressed by shifting by two bits, the configured value
2547:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT, and describes the number of bytes that are
2548:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    consumed from managed memory from which SystemView can calculate
2549:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    accurate heap metrics.
2550:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** */
2551:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** void SEGGER_SYSVIEW_HeapAlloc(void *pHeap, void* pUserData, unsigned int UserDataLen) {
