2564:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** 
2565:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** /*********************************************************************
2566:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2567:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *       SEGGER_SYSVIEW_HeapAllocEx()
2568:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2569:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Function description
2570:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Record a per-heap allocation event.
2571:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2572:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Parameters
2573:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    pHeap       - Pointer to heap where allocation was made.
2574:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    pUserData   - Pointer to allocated user data.
2575:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    UserDataLen - Size of block allocated to hold user data, excluding any metadata.
2576:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    Tag         - Block tag, typically used to identify the owner of the block.
2577:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2578:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  Additional information
2579:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    The user data must be correctly aligned for the architecture, which
2580:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    typically requires that the alignment is at least the alignment
2581:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of a double or a long long.  pUserData is, therefore, compressed by
2582:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    shrinking as IDs are compressed, controlled by the specific setting
ARM GAS  /var/folders/yl/_q9l42k90g1g4mdhbs226msm0000gn/T//ccxj18A8.s 			page 216


2583:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT.
2584:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2585:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    In the same way, UserDataLen must reflect the size of the allocated
2586:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    block, not the allocation size requested by the application.  This
2587:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    size is also subject to compression, controlled by the specific setting
2588:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT.
2589:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2590:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    As an example, assume the allocator is running on a Cortex-M device
2591:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    with SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT set to 2 (the word alignment of the device).
2592:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    If a user requests an allocation of 5 bytes, a hypothetical heap
2593:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    allocator could allocate a block with size 32 bytes for this.  The value
2594:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of UserDataLen sent to SystemView for recording should be 32, not 5,
2595:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    and the 32 is compressed by shifting by two bits, the configured value
2596:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    of SEGGER_SYSVIEW_ID_SHIFT, and describes the number of bytes that are
2597:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    consumed from managed memory from which SystemView can calculate
2598:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    accurate heap metrics.
2599:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *
2600:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *  See also
2601:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** *    SEGGER_SYSVIEW_HeapAlloc().
2602:./SystemView/SEGGER_SYSVIEW.c **** */
